-- title:
--   Finite exact output of the intended Algorithm 1
-- statement:
--   For each ring-valued $2\times2$ unitary $U$, define its squared-entry height from its upper-left entry, assigning height zero to the monomial case before taking an exponent of a zero entry. Build the small-height lookup by breadth-first enumeration of chronological H/T words. At height above three, test $k=0,1,2,3$ once each and take the first reduction $V\mapsto HT^{-k}V$ that lowers the height by one. Reconstruct chronological output by placing the recursive residual word before the suffix $H,T^k$.
--
--   There is an input-independent natural number $B$ such that every small-height lookup succeeds by BFS level $B$, and every valid input has a finite execution trace of this recipe with returned word $A(U)$ satisfying
--
--   $$
--   \forall U\in U(2)\cap R^{2\times2},\qquad M(A(U))=U.
--   $$
--
--   The trace follows only reducing steps and successful base lookups; the fallback branches are not used on valid inputs. This gives exact finite synthesis with a constructed table. The printed inner while-loop is replaced by the guarded single test required by the surrounding proof; this correction requires independent moderation. No bit-cost assertion is included here.
-- source:
--   Fast and efficient exact synthesis of single qubit unitaries generated by Clifford and T gates, arXiv:1206.5236v4, PDF p. 8, Algorithm 1 / §4 unnumbered main result: finite exact synthesis output

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Support21_P13

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Support21.P13

open scoped Classical

/-- Algorithm 1 output promise, PDF pp.7-8, with the explicitly disclosed
single-test repair in synthesisFuel. The base lookup is built by BFS. A global
finite cutoff precedes every input, so a correct finite table is a conclusion,
not an input oracle. No arithmetic or bit-runtime assertion is made here. -/
theorem algorithm1_correct :
    ∃ B : ℕ, ∀ U : Matrix Bool Bool ℂ,
      U ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup Bool ℂ → EntriesInRing U →
      (matrixHeight U ≤ 3 → baseDepth U ≤ B ∧
        htWordMatrix (baseWord U) = U) ∧
      SynthesisTrace B U (algorithm1 U) ∧ htWordMatrix (algorithm1 U) = U := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Support21.P13

end
